## Assumptions

| # | Assumption | Impact if Wrong |
|---|---|---|
| A-01 | NGO has a Razorpay account (or can create one) | Cannot process payments |
| A-02 | NGO team has email access for admin login | Cannot authenticate |
| A-03 | Target donors have smartphone/computer + internet | Cannot reach donors |
| A-04 | Indian donors primarily (INR, UPI, Indian cards) | Payment methods mismatch |
| A-05 | Single cause active at any time | UI design is simpler |
| A-06 | < 1000 donations/month initially | Free tier sufficient |
| A-07 | NGO doesn't need real-time notifications | No push/email alerts |
| A-08 | Supabase free tier is sufficient for MVP | No cost |
| A-09 | Vercel free tier is sufficient for hosting | No cost |

---

## Constraints

| # | Constraint | Type | Impact |
|---|---|---|---|
| C-01 | Test mode only (no real money) | Business | Limited to demo/POC |
| C-02 | Single developer + AI agent | Resource | Sequential development |
| C-03 | Free tier services (Supabase, Vercel) | Budget | Service limits apply |
| C-04 | No backend server (serverless only) | Technical | Cold start latency |
| C-05 | Razorpay India-only for test mode | Geographic | India-focused |
| C-06 | No CI/CD pipeline for MVP | Process | Manual deployment |

---

## Risks

| # | Risk | Probability | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| R-01 | Razorpay API downtime | Low | High | Error handling + retry + user message |
| R-02 | Supabase free tier limits exceeded | Low | Medium | Monitor usage, upgrade if needed |
| R-03 | Webhook delivery failure | Low | High | Razorpay retries for 24h, idempotent handling |
| R-04 | Payment reconciliation mismatch | Low | High | Dual verification (client verify + webhook) |
| R-05 | Admin credentials compromised | Low | High | Strong passwords, session expiry |
| R-06 | Donor data breach | Very Low | Critical | RLS, server-only secrets, HTTPS |

